Z||000005||batboy||09-29-1999||12:06 AM||||We talk about hotrodding our Fieros all the time and since you mentioned computer upgrades, well... I've hotrodded my custom built computer. In computer geek terms it's called overclocking. I have a Intel Celeron 300 MHz CPU chip (4.5X locked multiplier) that I'm running on a 100 MHz bus speed (normally 66 MHz) which produces a clock speed of 450 MHz. More power in true hotrod tradition. Anybody else in the forum tried overclocking their computers? This is actually my third successful overclocking attempt and my best. I've been running this setup since last February.||||reg||1
