Z||000009||Patrick||09-29-1999||03:34 AM||||<BR>Hey Cliff, I'm one notch up on you. I have my C366 running stable at <B>567 MHz</B> at 2.0 volts. I tried it at 612 MHz, but even at 2.3 volts it wouldn't load Windows.<P>My other hobby, besides keeping the Fiero running, is shooting and editing video. With non-linear editing, you can't beat brute processing power for rendering.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000010||batboy||09-29-1999||07:50 AM||||Cooling is always a concern when you're overclocking. I have a triple fan and massive heat sink on my CPU), a front case fan, and an expansion slot fan in the back. Of course, it also has the normal power supply fan too. Wow, you guys or getting 550 or better out of a Celery 366? I'm impressed! I've got my 300A to run 464 using the turbo mode on my Abit BH6, but never could run it stable at 504 MHz. It would boot, but then lock up in the windows start-up everytime.||||reg||1
